<title>FRANCE: AGF 883 mln Ffr gain on share sales.</title>
<headline>AGF 883 mln Ffr gain on share sales.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Insurance group Assurances Generales de France (AGF) said it had sold 2.75 billion francs of shares from its participations in other companies, generating a capital gain of 883 million francs.</p>
<p>A company official said AGF had sold shares in Total, Schneider, Rhone-Poulenc, Pinault-Printemps and re-insurer SCOR.</p>
<p>On the occasion of AGF's privatisation last May, it said it would sell between five and seven billion francs of shares from its stakes within 24 months.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
